CHECK:AVOID_EXTERNS: extern prototypes should be avoided in .h files
#113: FILE: drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_drv.h:1630:
+extern int intel_resume_force_mode(struct drm_device *dev);

Function prototypes don't need to be declared extern in .h
files.  It's assumed by the compiler and is unnecessary.

WARNING:CONST_STRUCT: struct drm_encoder_helper_funcs should normally be const
#129: FILE: drivers/gpu/drm/i915/intel_display.c:9003:
+	struct drm_encoder_helper_funcs *encoder_funcs;

Using const is generally a good idea.  Checkpatch reads
a list of frequently used structs that are always or
almost always constant.

The existing structs list can be viewed from
`scripts/const_structs.checkpatch`.

See: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/alpine.DEB.2.10.1608281509480.3321@hadrien/

CHECK:BRACES: Blank lines aren't necessary after an open brace '{'
#134: FILE: drivers/gpu/drm/i915/intel_display.c:9008:
+	list_for_each_entry(crtc, &dev->mode_config.crtc_list, head) {
+

The placement of braces is stylistically incorrect.
The preferred way is to put the opening brace last on the line,
and put the closing brace first::

  if (x is true) {
          we do y
  }

This applies for all non-functional blocks.
However, there is one special case, namely functions: they have the
opening brace at the beginning of the next line, thus::

  int function(int x)
  {
          body of function
  }

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#placing-braces-and-spaces

CHECK:BOOL_COMPARISON: Using comparison to false is error prone
#143: FILE: drivers/gpu/drm/i915/intel_display.c:9017:
+		if (ret == false)

Comparisons of A to true and false are better written
as A and !A.

See: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/1365563834.27174.12.camel@joe-AO722/

